Notes for spec phase (Option A v1 calibration):
- Original chainring hypothesis was houghR/aimR > ~1.4 -> conf=0 abstain.
  Observed range [0.39, 1.15] does NOT contain >1.4 in this 10-photo cohort.
  Two interpretations:
  (a) Smoke uses rMap[peakI] which is last-wins per cell -- not the true peak
      radius; production must use 3D accumulator (cx, cy, r) for accurate radius.
  (b) 2D collapse + both-polarity voting saturates the inner-circle bin; the
      large-gear case (42T+) shows houghR clustering at ~160-185 (similar to
      inner BCD circle in chainring images, not the outer tooth tips).
- Spec must therefore CALIBRATE on a stratified n>=45 sweep BEFORE choosing the
  discriminator predicate. Candidate predicates to evaluate:
  * R1: houghR > tau1 * min(W,H) absolute large-circle floor
  * R2: peakVotes / edgeCount > tau2 (signal-strength gate)
  * R3: 3D accumulator full radius distribution (defer if R1/R2 sufficient)
- Earliest-cheapest first: smoke uses 2D + per-vote rMap; if calibration shows
  R1/R2 insufficient, fall back to 3D accumulator (still cheap: peak found via
  argmax over flat array; same edge x radius cost).
